<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  WookieeHead_Upgrade.xml                    Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-11
  ============================================================================

  WHAT THIS DOES
  ==============
  Swaps one gene in the BTD_Wookiee xenotype so Wookiees use Outer Rim's
  512x512 head art instead of Star Wars Xenotypes' 128x128 art.

      guy762_Head_wookiee   ==>   OuterRim_WookieeHead

  THE FINDING  [VERIFIED 2026-08-11 against the live DefDump, 2026-08-11T16:25Z]
  ============================================================================
  Two complete, correctly-authored Wookiee head chains exist in this stack.
  NEITHER IS BUGGY - both are properly gated with requiredGenes, so neither
  pollutes the open head pool. The difference is purely which art they point at:

    GeneDef OuterRim_WookieeHead        [Outer Rim - Galactic Diversity]
      forcedHeadTypes: OuterRim_Wookiee
      HeadTypeDef OuterRim_Wookiee
        graphicPath  : Things/Pawn/Humanlike/Heads/Wookiee/Wookiee
        requiredGenes: OuterRim_WookieeHead
        measured     : 512 x 512, south / north / east

    GeneDef guy762_Head_wookiee         [Star Wars Xenotypes]
      forcedHeadTypes: Wookiee_Average1, Wookiee_Average2, Wookiee_Average3
      HeadTypeDef Wookiee_Average1..3
        graphicPath  : Pawn/HeadType/wookiee/wookiee1..3
        requiredGenes: Furskin, guy762_Head_wookiee
        measured     : 128 x 128, south / north / east

  Every other species in the Star Wars Xenotypes pack ships at 512x512. The
  Wookiee is the single outlier in that mod, at a quarter the linear resolution.

  WHY THE XENOTYPE PICKED THE WORSE ONE
  =====================================
  BTD_Wookiee comes from [BTD] Xenotype REMIX: Star Wars, the mod adopted
  specifically to dedupe the Star Wars Xenotypes / Outer Rim overlap. Its own
  BTD_Data/XenotypeEquivalencies.xml names all three Wookiee xenotypes as one
  species group:

      <EquivalentGroup>
        <Species>Wookiee</Species>
        <BTD>BTD_Wookiee</BTD>
        <SWX>guy762_xenotype_wookiee</SWX>
        <OR>OuterRim_Wookiee</OR>
      </EquivalentGroup>

  So it knew both existed and resolved to the lower-resolution art. That is a
  judgement call by its author, not a defect - which is exactly why a local
  patch is the right remedy rather than a bug report.

  THE TRADE-OFF  (deliberate, accepted)
  =====================================
  Star Wars Xenotypes ships THREE head variants; Outer Rim ships ONE. After
  this patch every Wookiee shares a head. Accepted because at 128 px the three
  variants are barely distinguishable, and 4x linear resolution is the larger
  visual win. Revisit if Wookiees ever become numerous enough for the sameness
  to read as a bug.

  WHAT THIS PATCH DOES NOT DO
  ===========================
  * It does not touch guy762_xenotype_wookiee or OuterRim_Wookiee - only the
    BTD (deduped) xenotype, which is the one this playthrough spawns.
  * It does not add body art. None is missing: Furskin is a Biotech gene whose
    renderNodeProperties attach a PawnRenderNode_Fur to the Body tag, so the
    fur IS the body treatment. BTD_Wookiee already carries Furskin.
    (An earlier audit called this a missing-texture gap. That was wrong - it
    looked for a BodyType/wookiee folder and read absence as absence of art.)

  SAFETY
  ======
  Nested conditionals: the outer one confirms the REPLACEMENT gene exists
  before anything is removed, so if Outer Rim - Galactic Diversity is ever
  disabled this whole operation becomes a silent no-op rather than stripping
  the Wookiee's head gene and leaving it headless. The inner one confirms the
  gene we intend to remove is actually present, so re-running or a future
  upstream fix also degrades to a no-op.

  Load Jawa_Patches LAST, after both Star Wars Xenotypes and Outer Rim.

  VERIFY AFTER THE NEXT LOAD
  ==========================
  1. Dev-mode spawn a BTD_Wookiee pawn; the head should be visibly crisper.
  2. Check all three facings - the east profile is where the 128px version is
     worst and the improvement is most obvious.
  3. grep Player.log for  "Failed to find any textures at"  and for
     "OuterRim_WookieeHead"  - neither should appear as an error.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <!-- Outer Rim's head gene must exist before we depend on it. -->
    <xpath>/Defs/GeneDef[defName="OuterRim_WookieeHead"]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
      <!-- And the gene we are replacing must actually be in the list. -->
      <xpath>/Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="BTD_Wookiee"]/genes/li[text()="guy762_Head_wookiee"]</xpath>
      <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
        <operations>

          <li Class="PatchOperationRemove">
            <xpath>/Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="BTD_Wookiee"]/genes/li[text()="guy762_Head_wookiee"]</xpath>
          </li>

          <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
            <xpath>/Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="BTD_Wookiee"]/genes</xpath>
            <value>
              <li>OuterRim_WookieeHead</li>
            </value>
          </li>

        </operations>
      </match>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
